{"items":[{"recordId":"teach-generated-31acc1481df1ab2f","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"source","text":"An application fan is a triangular net agent: its principal port connects to the function, its first auxiliary port to the result or parent, and its second auxiliary port to the argument.","requires":[],"citationRequired":true}]},{"recordId":"teach-generated-209163225799547c","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"source","text":"A function fan is the abstraction-oriented form of a triangular net agent, called an abstraction fan in the source: its ports represent the parent, the function body, and the bound variable.","requires":[],"citationRequired":true}]}]}
